WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.775
Many production . NET containers run under an orchestrator such as Kubernetes, Azure Container Apps, Docker Swarm, or another platform.

2
00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:16.416
Even when platform teams own the cluster, developers should understand the controls that shape application behavior.

3
00:00:16.416 --> 00:00:19.442
The app and the platform settings need to agree.

4
00:00:19.442 --> 00:00:27.309
Security context settings can define user identity, privilege behavior, filesystem settings, and capability handling.

5
00:00:27.309 --> 00:00:41.607
Where applicable, settings such as runAsNonRoot, runAsUser, allowPrivilegeEscalation, capabilities, privileged mode, and readOnlyRootFilesystem should be reviewed against what the application actually requires.

6
00:00:41.607 --> 00:00:47.507
Resource requests and limits protect platform stability and application predictability.

7
00:00:47.507 --> 00:00:50.079
Requests help the scheduler place work.

8
00:00:50.079 --> 00:00:55.526
Limits help prevent one workload from consuming capacity that other workloads need.

9
00:00:55.526 --> 00:01:04.225
. NET applications should be tested under realistic memory and CPU constraints so failures are understandable rather than surprising.

10
00:01:04.225 --> 00:01:14.060
Service accounts, RBAC, namespaces, network policies, secrets, config maps, admission controls, and image pull policies all affect runtime security.

11
00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:19.506
A workload should receive only the platform permissions and network access it needs.

12
00:01:19.506 --> 00:01:25.936
Configuration and secret objects should have clear ownership, review, and rotation expectations.

13
00:01:25.936 --> 00:01:41.671
Probes need careful design. Liveness and readiness probes should help the platform route traffic and recover unhealthy instances, but they should not hide dependency failures, trigger unnecessary restart loops, or expose detailed internals.

14
00:01:41.671 --> 00:01:49.614
Applications should behave predictably under restricted pod settings and should not require broad host access by default.
